            <ArticleTitle>Cerebellar atrophy in epilepsy and headache: lack of relationship to phenytoin.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>910-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>CT scans of 70 patients with seizures and 48 patients with headaches were studied. Using accepted CT criteria for the diagnosis of cerebellar atrophy, the films were analyzed in a blind, unbiased fashion to evaluate possible relationship between cerebellar atrophy and phenytoin use or epilepsy itself. We found no evidence that either phenytoin or epilepsy caused cerebellar atrophy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
